YAAP Ran-Elf-Mal-Cha
artiwishless, polyselfless, polypileless

This is another ascension in my alphabetic series, that started with
Arc and this time got to Ranger. Unlike the previous role, Priest,
number of games were needed to suceed, most of them very silly early
deaths, but also more memorable ones, like a game where I diluted
potions in a fountain and summoned water demon summarily executed my
characted with wand of death.

1) I dived into the Mines first, reached Minetown, but further
progress was halted by gnome with a wand of lightning. There was magic
lamp in the Minetown tools shop and later I found another one.

2) I found a shield of reflection in an armor shop, which guaranteed
that I got amulet of reflection in Sokoban.

3) With reflection I finished the Mines, where I found tinning kit.

4) Found wizard bones on dlvl 8, with some good stuff (mainly CoMR and
+5 ring of protection)

5) There was coaligned temple on dlvl 9, my very first sacrifice
yielded Stormbringer.

6) Used spare magic lamp to wish for a bag of holding. This was good
thing to do, since I never saw another one in this game.

7) After I was able to bless things, I blessed stack of 10 scrolls of
identify, second of which identified all my stuff, which included ring
of teleport control, ring of polymorph control, ring of slow
digestion. I could also uncurse the ring of protection from bones.

8) Till this point I have accumulated two tins of tengu meat. I ate
them and experienced the luckiest moment of the entire game: the first
one gave me teleport control, the second one gave me teleportitis. The
probability of this happening is 3.4%!

9) On dlvl 13 I run into an air elemental hiding around a corner and
only narrowly escaped by teleporting out.

10) Medusa and Castle were uneventful, I was using +5 boots of
levitation I found somewhere (not bones!)

11) Valley of the Dead was quite challenging, as there was monster
summoning demilich. Standing on E I was safe, but it was getting
little protracted. At least I had chance to get two stalker meat tins
to get finally invisible.

12) After consolidating my stash to VoTD, wishing for GDSM and speed
boots and enchanting stuff, I embarked on my Quest with ascension-
grade AC of -31. The quest was easy and straightforward, Scorpius did
last whole four blows from my +6 Stormbringer. I got two genocides
from the Scorpius throne, so I genocided disenchanters and green
slimes (the usual L, h and ; were already genocided).

13) I wished for a robe in order to be able spellcast magic mapping
(robe makes big difference to ranger's spellcasting).

14) Gehennom was straightforward due to my high AC and magic mapping.
I skipped Orcus to return to it from below and trice corpse, but in
fact, it never came along. Eventually I got cockatrice on the Orcus
level and used it to stone him (he managed to waste two charges,
unfortunately). Vlad killed himself by zapping wand of fire at me.

15) As I did not have unholy water I had to rely on confused scrolls
of teleportation. This caused me quite some grief since I did not
realize I must not be stunned for teleport control to work. Also there
were some inherent misses. Anyway, after some 6 scrolls of
teleportation, I finally got to the top of Wizard's Tower.

16) I had extreme trouble finding the doors to the Moloch's Sanctum. I
used detect unseen spell, which for some reason I don't understand,
failed to reveal the doors location. After circling the Sanctum three
times I had to use stethoscope to find the door (wading in the fire
traps, of course). Fortunately, Rodney was occupied by arguing with
the high priest about who is to keep the Amulet.

17) After finally getting the Amulet, I started to run up. Mysterious
force seemed worse than when I was lawful, extremely annoying. Also
Rodney kept appearing, even stealing the Amulet once. Fortunately, he
summoned cockatrice so I could stone him promptly.

18) On the Plane of Air I switched from speed boots to levitation
boots and quaffed blessed potion of speed. I managed to avoid all the
E's, which was good, my maxHP was only about 161.

19) The Astral Plane was quick -- I avoided the usual tour of all
altars as the first one was the right one. Those +6 poisoned arrows
were quite useful in killing stuff on the Astral Plane and I even had
some instakills due to poison and killed Famine twice from afar, like
a true Ranger!

What this game did not provide: wand of cancellation, wand of
polymorph, magic whistle (found one very late in the game), scroll of
taming, ring of levitation, ring of free action. My smoky potion was
polymorph, which I only saw once.

